<section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><div class="legacy-content"><h1>Keeping you informed</h1>

<h3>- The CMA are suggesting all Suppliers have access to your details </h3>
<article>
    <p>
        The Competition and Markets Authority have had an energy markets investigation under way since June 2014.
        One of the proposals is to allow Other Suppliers access to your details with your current supplier.  The
        idea is (perhaps) that these Other Suppliers can contact you and offer you a better deal than the one you
        are on.  Well ... of course they will!  They are ALL going to suggest that you switch to them and leave your
        current supplier; its a no-brainer!
    </p>
    <p>
        Not only is it insecure and unsafe, this proposal is also a complete waste of time, because the ONLY way these
        Other Suppliers can REALLY offer you a better deal is to do what SmartSwitch does and analyze your bills.  Your
        current supplier won't give them access to your usage because that is 'company confidential'.  So
        without using SmartSwitch (which they don't have) you will be inundated with unqualifiable, unproven
        offers which you cannot corroborate independently.  Only SmartSwitch performs an independent, unbiased analysis
        of your energy usage and only SmartSwitch gives you the ONE supplier who is the cheapest.
    </p>
    <p>
        SmartSwitch took FIFTEEN YEARS to create; it's not a bit of Javascript knocked up by a spotty kid in 10 minutes
        to 'guess' your cheapest supplier - anyone can do that.
    </p>
    <p>
        Its not magic - its logic!  <span style="color:red">Smart</span><span style="color:deepskyblue">Switch!</span> does the maths for you!
    </p>
</article>

<h3>- Ofgem targets everybody ... except us! </h3>
<article>
    <p>
        You may have read in the news that Ofgem has begun an investigation into whether or not all
        the price comparison websites (PCWs) have breached competition law by sharing details of
        commission rates they charge suppliers.
        <a href="http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-3111706/Comparison-site-shares-plummet-watchdog-starts-probe-Millions-wiped-value-named-inquiry-market-rigging.html?ITO=1490&ns_mchannel=rss&ns_campaign=1490" title="Read all about it!"></a>
        In the recent past the PCWs have been accused of 'holding
        back' or not showing cheap tariffs from suppliers when there is no commission to be gained
        by switching consumers to them.
        This is despite the fact that the majority of these PCWs are Ofgem accredited
        and proudly display the Ofgem logo to that effect!
    </p>
    <p>
        Whilst all the PCWs are in denial over this matter, here at SmartCubeMobile we sleep soundly
        and softly in our beds at night!  We have never had ANY relationship with any energy supplier or for
        that matter any PCW and we neither receive nor give commission or any other payments to any
        other enterprise.  You can be 1000% sure that the prices you see on OUR website are free from bias and
        fair - and that is <i>GUARANTEED!</i>
    </p>
    <p>
        Will Ofgem ever investigate us?  No, never, because we are free and independent of all suppliers
    </p>
    <p>
        Will Ofgem ever query our relationships with other PCWs?  No because we don't talk to them nor they to us
    </p>
    <p>
        Its not magic - its logic!  <span style="color:red">Smart</span><span style="color:deepskyblue">Switch!</span> does the maths for you!
    </p>
</article>

<h3>- Age UK are in hot water ... but it will never happen to us! </h3>
<article>
    <p>
        You may have heard on the radio or the television that Age UK have been taking commission payments of up to
        £60 from E-On to switch vulnerable and trusting elderly people to uncompetitive tariffs.  This is
        because neither Age UK (nor E-On for that matter) have access to SmartSwitch.  It simply isn't possible
        to determine which tariff someone could possibly switch to without examining (at least) their past usage
        in detail.
    </p>
    <p>
        To whom - or when - or to what - you switch to depends on where you are, what you use and how you pay (the 'Big 3')
        and the results might well differ even for two old age pensioners living alone in adjacent terraced houses.
        Age UK has recommended their flawed switching process - with the complicity of E-On - because neither of these
        organizations have performed the type of simple analysis that SmartSwitch performs.
    </p>
    <p>
        Will we ever be on the radio or television in such a pickle?  No, never, because we are free and independent of all suppliers
        (and even organizations such as Age UK for that matter).
    </p>
    <p>
        We have created SmartSwitch to benefit old fogeys such as ourselves.
    </p>
    <p>
        Its not magic - its logic!  <span style="color:red">Smart</span><span style="color:deepskyblue">Switch!</span> does the maths for you!
